n other barbarian rulers in winning the loyalty of the defeated peoples. Like many of their predecessers such as Shi Le, the Wei rulers distinguished between a core element in their state, the so-called "compatriots" (guoren), and the mass of ordinary subjects. Almost all military commands and other positions of real power and authority were held by compatriots." <br>However, what does this argue?<br>Dai Wei Hong. 2010. Investigation of the Merit System of the Northern Wei Dynasty'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 918, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 762})
