icials (provincial governor level) had to be ethnic Inca, however there were exceptions.  There was some degree of merit promotion.<br>"Inka rulers began to appoint close relatives to religious, administrative, and military positions." <br>Inca of Privilege could hold roles in the government administration and leadership positions like provincial governor. <br>Commoners could rise to become top administrators and military leaders. '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 928, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 797})
